# Cloudflare Workers Assets reads this file from the assets root.
#
# Without it, HTML and static assets get identical treatment: everything is
# revalidated on every repeat view, so a warm second visit to /services issues
# roughly twenty conditional requests where it should issue one.

# Security headers, every response. An audit on 2026-09-01 scored these 0 of 6
# and a live check on 2026-10-31 found all six still absent.
#
# The CSP is strict rather than permissive because this site earned the right to
# one: every script, style, font, image and media file is same-origin. A sweep of
# all 153 pages found ZERO external script, style, iframe or font origins - the
# only absolute URLs in the HTML are this site's own canonical and og tags. There
# are no iframes, no inline event handlers, no javascript: hrefs, and one local
# script. So default-src 'self' costs nothing here.
#
# Three deliberate loosenings, each with a reason rather than a shrug:
#   style-src 'unsafe-inline' - every page carries a <style> block and there are
#     8 style="" attributes. Hashing 153 blocks that change with the content would
#     break on the next edit, silently, which is worse than this.
#   img-src data: - inlined SVG icons.
#   JSON-LD needs no allowance: application/ld+json is data, never executed, so
#     script-src does not apply to it.
#
# connect-src 'self' is safe because main.js makes no fetch or XHR at all; the
# one external reference in it builds a wa.me LINK, which is navigation and not
# subject to connect-src. form-action 'self' is safe because all 157 forms carry
# no action attribute and are handled in JS.
#
# HSTS omits includeSubDomains and preload on purpose. A client site is scheduled
# to move onto a subdomain of this host, and committing every future subdomain to
# HTTPS-only before it exists is how a launch breaks at the worst moment. The
# max-age alone is what the audit scores.
/*
  Strict-Transport-Security: max-age=31536000
  X-Content-Type-Options: nosniff
  Referrer-Policy: strict-origin-when-cross-origin
  X-Frame-Options: SAMEORIGIN
  Permissions-Policy: camera=(), microphone=(), geolocation=(), payment=(), usb=()
  Content-Security-Policy: default-src 'self'; script-src 'self'; style-src 'self' 'unsafe-inline'; img-src 'self' data:; font-src 'self'; connect-src 'self'; media-src 'self'; object-src 'none'; frame-ancestors 'self'; base-uri 'self'; form-action 'self'; upgrade-insecure-requests

# Fonts are content-addressed by name in practice - a different cut would be a
# different filename - so they can be cached hard. Immutable means the browser
# will not even revalidate.
/assets/fonts/*
  Cache-Control: public, max-age=31536000, immutable
  Access-Control-Allow-Origin: *

# Images and video: long-lived but NOT immutable. These filenames are stable
# rather than hashed, so replacing an image in place has to remain possible.
# Thirty days is long enough to help repeat visitors and short enough that a
# swapped photo reaches them without a rename.
/assets/img/*
  Cache-Control: public, max-age=2592000

/assets/video/*
  Cache-Control: public, max-age=2592000

# CSS and JS carry a ?v= query that changes on every edit, so a long max-age is
# safe: a new version is a new URL as far as the browser cache is concerned.
# Deliberately NOT immutable, because the query is not part of the path, so any
# intermediary that strips query strings would otherwise serve a year-stale
# file. Hashed filenames would let this be immutable; the query trick does not.
/assets/css/*
  Cache-Control: public, max-age=604800

/assets/js/*
  Cache-Control: public, max-age=604800

# HTML must always be revalidated, or a content fix would not reach anyone
# holding a cached copy. The ETag makes the common case a cheap 304.
/*.html
  Cache-Control: public, max-age=0, must-revalidate

/
  Cache-Control: public, max-age=0, must-revalidate

# These describe the site to crawlers and change with the content, so they are
# revalidated too rather than pinned.
/sitemap.xml
  Cache-Control: public, max-age=3600

/robots.txt
  Cache-Control: public, max-age=3600

/llms.txt
  Cache-Control: public, max-age=3600
